## Sequencing and capacity

The first product target is .1 → .3 → .4 → .5: a reliable internal draft with
no business-system connection dependency. Context .2 supplies the useful
company/workspace inputs; it can be built alongside action contracts once .1
is verified. Later integration nodes use synthetic adapters while source
owners complete real applications.

Planning allowance: 8–12 engineering weeks for the first governed internal
release and synthetic integration acceptance, assuming one full-time core
engineer working with AI Builders, existing source access and no major baseline
regression. This is an unvalidated planning range, not a deadline or measured
AI execution-time estimate. Reestimate after .1 and .4a. Actual connector
owner readiness, live data validation and production rollout are additional
dependencies. Standard is demonstrated by acceptance, not by calendar.

Use roughly 60% capacity for the next vertical slice, 25% for source integrity,
reliability and performance, and 15% for user feedback/unplanned findings.
Prefer fewer complete workflows over simultaneous unfinished integrations.

