## TIP-054.1 · Baseline and recovery closure

Priority P0. Dependencies: approved Blueprint. Requirements EOS-001/002/016/031.
Reuse current specialist services. Verify actual serving build/config separately
from report headers. Reproduce document DB→Redis and stale-render crash seams
in an isolated local environment, then repair only demonstrated gaps.

Given a committed render job and a failed queue publication, when service/queue
recover, then the same job is dispatched and exactly one valid artifact is
registered. Given worker death during rendering, when its ownership expires,
then work recovers or reports an actionable terminal state instead of remaining
silently stuck. Given the new IDF retrieval baseline, ordinary noisy/follow-up
questions still answer their real subject. Validate `use_class` for every
new disclosure/draft surface and preserve useful partial evidence behavior.

Evidence: crash-injection traces, duplicate-output query, unit/integration
regression, migration/restore checks if schema changes, focused browser state.
Live internal-evidence synthesis is a separate bounded authorized campaign.

Execution status: local criteria BRC-001…008 verified on schema 0016 and
uncommitted source. Backend 894 passed / 17 explicit skips; web 220 passed;
five mocked browser cases passed. Serving identity/provider latency are not
certified. See [current implementation status](IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md) and
[Contractor Verify](../../vibecode_v2/TIP-054.1_VERIFY_REPORT.md). Remaining
nodes below are planned, not implemented by this recovery milestone.

## TIP-054.2 · Company context and workspace memory

Priority P0. Dependencies .1. Requirements EOS-002/008/009/010/011/024.
Output: canonical entity relations, temporal ownership/source refs,
`ContextPacket`, scoped memory lifecycle and domain coverage/freshness view.
Keep SOT and source APIs authoritative. Add PostgreSQL structures only where
existing records cannot express the required lifecycle.

Given permitted current and stale/missing context, when a project goal is
planned, then the packet includes supported context, exact revisions and
explicit gaps. Given revoked/deleted evidence, when remembered context is
reused, then it cannot disclose that evidence. Given a remembered preference,
it cannot become a permission or company fact. Correction/deletion is visible.

Evidence: entity collision, revision drift, temporal validity, context budget,
permission/memory expiry and deletion tests; relevance/coverage holdout cases.

Execution status: CTX-001…009 pass in the governed-SOT/API/memory slice;
15 unit and 23 SQL integration scenarios. No Ask/UI integration, live state
connector or company-wide coverage certification. See
[.2/.3 Contractor Verify](../../vibecode_v2/TIP-054.2_054.3_VERIFY_REPORT.md).

## TIP-054.3 · Action Kernel contracts

Priority P0. Dependencies .1. Requirements EOS-003/007/012/013/014/015/027/030.
Output: typed capability registry, action plans, policy-action mapping,
approval/receipt/event models and domain persistence. Reuse PolicyEngine,
UnitOfWork, AuditRepository, budgets and resource identities.

Given a normal read, the caller's existing rights suffice. Given an explicit
internal-draft request, no additional per-tool confirmation is inserted.
Given a tool requesting a higher-risk effect, only its admitted permissions
apply. Changed input/version/recipient invalidates the previous approval.
Model-generated tool names/parameters outside the admitted contract fail before
effects; an error identifies a useful permitted continuation when available.

Evidence: schema and policy contracts; approval-binding adversarial tests;
correlated receipts; audit redaction; finite run-budget accounting.

Execution status: ACT-001…009 pass; 28 unit and 28 SQL/API scenarios. Fixed
R0/R1 admission contracts only; no executor, fake effect-success receipt or
live R2/R3 workflow. Combined frozen gates: backend 1,024 passed/17 explicit
skips; web 220 passed; populated migration, lint/types/build pass. Effect
activation still requires .4b, not inference from domain admission.

