## TIP-054.4b · Durable executor and business receipts

Priority P0. Dependencies .4a. Requirements EOS-007/010/014/015/016/017/018/019/
027/030/031. Output: selected runner adapter, isolated state, waits, cancel,
resume, step attempts, idempotency, reconciliation and outcome verification.

Given crash after a possible source effect, the system queries its source key
before a retry. A source without a safe query/idempotency mechanism returns
`needs_review`. Given two workers, stale ownership cannot commit a duplicate
result. Given approval revoked/expired while waiting, resumption rechecks.
Given partial irreversible work, cancellation reports completed effects and
remaining stopped steps accurately. Backup/restore retains pending waits and
receipts. Deployment-version migration supports paused workflows explicitly.

Evidence: fault-injection suite, deterministic receipt/state oracles, restart,
restore, worker fencing and workflow version tests, measured overhead.

Execution status: IMPLEMENTED / PARTIAL / NOT READY. Historical4c446 admits DBOS with unchanged serving
pins; real R0/R1, recovery/restore, current authority/output protection and
two-live-worker fencing pass finite synthetic tests. Backend 1,095 pass/17
explicit skips; Contractor's fresh64 independent reruns pass (overlap).
Actual source-wheel, populated migration and current-byte runtime proofs pass.
EXE-009 load remains FAIL after A/B/C: admission25/50 p95 768.3/1,511.3ms,
67/100 submit timeouts at50. Dedicated measured query-budget/batching design is
next; unchanged gates still apply. No local READY or
enterprise release GO is inferred. See
