## TIP-054.6 · MCP gateway

Priority P0. Dependencies .3/.4b/.5. Requirements EOS-010/014/018/021/022/023.
Output: official SDK adapter, server/tool admission, schema/version locking,
source identity/scopes, limits and fake-server tests. Read-only outbound first;
optional selected inbound capability exposure is separately configured.

Given an unapproved server, changed schema or wrong token audience, no call
executes. Given malicious instructions in tool output, they remain data and
cannot alter capability policy. Given an authenticated tool, caller/source
row/field scope still applies. Given no real source endpoint, UI reports ready
contract state instead of showing a connected system. Host risk class never
trusts annotations as permission. Reconcile ambiguous effects as .4b specifies.

Evidence: HTTP/auth/error contracts, schema drift, redirect/egress, scope
revocation, poisoned descriptions/results, fake timeouts and call-budget tests.

## TIP-054.7 · Operational read and SOT delta workflows

Priority P0. Dependencies .2/.5/.6. Requirements EOS-009/023/024/025.
Output: meeting preparation, CRM/MRP/IP source-read contracts and file-to-SOT
delta proposals. Keep adapters synthetic until actual source owner supplies
the authoritative endpoint/contract. Enable one real read model at a time.

Given authorized operating state, brief source timestamps and complete relevant
facts; stale feeds are explicit. Given new file facts, delta identifies new,
changed and conflicting values with evidence/owner review. Generated proposals
do not publish SOT. Given source deletions or denied fields, neither answer nor
draft can reveal the removed values. Transactional writes await specific scope.

Evidence: synthetic transaction oracles, field/row masks, freshness/deletion,
delta replay/idempotency, conflict and decision tests; real source canary only
after configuration and activation authorization.

## TIP-054.8 · Events, watches and governed proactivity

Priority P1. Dependencies .4b/.7. Requirements EOS-011/026/027/030.
Output: durable subscriptions, deduplicated source events, task/workspace
briefing drafts and rate/noise controls. Deliver through in-app activity first.
Slack/native-chat delivery remains a configured future adapter.

Given a duplicated/out-of-order event, one relevant proposal is produced with
accurate source state. Given no meaningful change, there is no repeated noisy
notification. Given revoked rights or expired subscription, scheduled work no
longer discloses content. Unsolicited external send/issue is never inferred
from the subscription to a briefing.

Evidence: event reorder/delete/replay, clock/expiry/restart, noise-rate,
budget/deduplication and user pause/resume tests.

## TIP-054.9 · Integrated acceptance and rollout packet

Priority P0. Dependencies all prior enabled slices. Requirements all 32,
especially EOS-001/002/005/006/028/031/032.
Output: exact build/runtime/schema/corpus/capability binding; applicable full
synthetic catalog, repeated usefulness holdout, latency/cost profile and honest
status for source/production dependencies.

Given a release candidate, all evidence cites its digest and exercised feature
flags. Given a failing critical policy/duplicate/false-success oracle, promotion
fails. Given AI-simulated review, report it as simulation; no human observation
is invented. Repeat defined stochastic trials without cherry-pick, retain all
failures, and compare cost per accepted outcome and p50/p95/p99. Existing Ask,
Files, Documents and Knowledge Ops remain in regression.

Local release and company-wide production GO are separate verdicts. Operator
production configuration/real-source acceptance and Homeowner GO are retained
when actual deployment is requested.

## Delivery protocol

Each application milestone gets its own detailed TIP before Builder starts,
Completion Report with changed files/AC results/issues/deviations, and
Contractor Verify with requirement coverage, scenarios, technical health and
READY/NOT READY. Known failures and deferrals remain visible. A source-level
risk does not become a confirmed defect until reproduced or proved by a
specific code path.

Commit/push/build identity is done at coherent verified milestones when
authorized. Documentation preparation does not modify the serving runtime.
Builders make routine implementation decisions within the approved contract;
changes to business effect scope or architecture return to Contractor/Homeowner.
